    "q-353079": {
      "dom_id": "step-q353079",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Compute the values of $\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi )$ for which the polar curve $r=2$ has a horizontal tangent, given that\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nThe polar curve has a horizontal tangent at $\\theta =$ \n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We have a horizontal tangent when\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the horizontal tangents, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Compute the derivatives ${y}^{′}(\\theta )$ and ${x}^{′}(\\theta ).$ \n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the values of $\\theta $ where ${y}^{′}(\\theta )=0.$\n\nBy writing down and solving the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ \\theta  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. However, among the solutions above, only one belongs to the required domain, namely\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Check to see whether our candidate has ${x}^{′}(\\theta )=0.$ \n\nWe substitute our candidate solution into ${x}^{′}(\\theta )$ and check that ${x}^{′}(\\theta )\\ne 0.$ If ${x}^{′}(\\theta )=0,$ further investigation is necessary.\n\n- Substituting ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-1) \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, our curve has a horizontal tangent at $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14227550/assets/515b40ad43d2299d0e8eb0521acee460b232794f488b4a0a7325b61516157bff.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
